IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcdd-dates`
IMPORT `wcdd-claims`

-- Workers' Compensation (Dust Diseases) Act 1942 (NSW) -- cases for every exported question in wcdd-claims.l4. Every
-- expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the encoding's output. Weekdays: 2, 5, 9,
-- 13 and 16 November 2026 are Monday, Thursday, Monday, Friday and Monday; 31 December 2026 is a Thursday and 1 January
-- 2027 (New Year's Day) a Friday.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website, via the Open Australian Legal Corpus
-- (version as at 18 October 2022). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases`

§§ `s 3, Sch 1 -- definitions`

#ASSERT `Is my disease a dust disease` `mesothelioma` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my disease a dust disease` `silicosis` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my disease a dust disease` `talcosis` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my disease a dust disease` `another condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum caused by dust that can also cause a listed disease` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my disease a dust disease` `some other disease or condition` EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker under the Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I the worker's spouse under the Act` `legally married to the worker` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the worker's spouse under the Act` `the worker's de facto partner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the worker's spouse under the Act` `the worker's de facto partner` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I the worker's spouse under the Act` `neither` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8(1)(a) -- the worker's award`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` `the panel certifies me totally disabled for work from a dust disease` TRUE `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` `the panel certifies me partially disabled for work from a dust disease` TRUE `a worker for only part of the time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` `the panel certifies me partially disabled for work from a dust disease` TRUE `a worker for only part of the time` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` `the panel certifies me totally disabled for work from a dust disease` TRUE `never a worker in that occupation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` `the panel has not certified me disabled for work from a dust disease` TRUE `a worker for the whole of the time` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to an award for my disablement` `the panel certifies me totally disabled for work from a dust disease` FALSE `a worker for the whole of the time` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8(1)(b), (c) -- the dependants' award`

-- Arguments: dependant; (b) certificate; (c)(i) receiving; applied; panel before death; worker time; part-time attribution; refused examination.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled under section 8(1)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled under section 8(1)(b), death from a dust disease`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for only part of the time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `entitled under section 8(1)(b), death from a dust disease`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for only part of the time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled under section 8(1)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease` `never a worker in that occupation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `entitled under section 8(1)(c), but the Authority may refuse all or part because they refused an examination`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the panel had not examined them but certifies after death that they were disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `entitled under section 8(1)(c), death of a person disabled by a dust disease`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the panel has not certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled under section 8(1)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease` `never a worker in that occupation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled under section 8(1)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled as a dependant after the death` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the panel examined them before death and certified them disabled from a dust disease` `a worker for the whole of the time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled under section 8(1)`

§§ `s 8(1A), (1AA) -- the 2 working days`

-- Thursday 5 November: Friday 6, Monday 9.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority decide my claim` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the date` 9 11 2026
-- The later is the information, Wednesday 11 November: Thursday 12, Friday 13.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority decide my claim` (`the date` 9 11 2026) (`the date` 11 11 2026) EQUALS `the date` 13 11 2026
-- Friday 13 November: Monday 16, Tuesday 17.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority decide my claim` (`the date` 13 11 2026) (`the date` 13 11 2026) EQUALS `the date` 17 11 2026
-- Saturday 14 and Sunday 15 November: Monday 16, Tuesday 17.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority decide my claim` (`the date` 14 11 2026) (`the date` 1 11 2026) EQUALS `the date` 17 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority decide my claim` (`the date` 15 11 2026) (`the date` 1 11 2026) EQUALS `the date` 17 11 2026
-- Thursday 31 December 2026: Friday 1 January 2027 counts (fork F7: public holidays not skipped), then Monday 4 January.
#ASSERT `By when must the Authority decide my claim` (`the date` 31 12 2026) (`the date` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the date` 4 1 2027

#ASSERT `Was my claim decided in time` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 9 11 2026) (`the date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `decided within the 2 working days`
#ASSERT `Was my claim decided in time` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 10 11 2026) (`the date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `decided late, but the decision is not invalid for that reason`
#ASSERT `Was my claim decided in time` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `decided within the 2 working days`
#ASSERT `Was my claim decided in time` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the date` 4 11 2026) (`the date` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `decided within the 2 working days`
#ASSERT `Was my claim decided in time` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 9 11 2026) EQUALS `not yet decided, and the 2 working days have not ended`
#ASSERT `Was my claim decided in time` (`the date` 5 11 2026) (`the date` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 10 11 2026) EQUALS `not yet decided, and the 2 working days have ended`

